====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  If res-V's cosine recovers toward 1 while its width stays well under
  the linear register's M+N, the aliasing diagnosis is confirmed AND the
  fix is worth porting into _design_spec as an optional extra-rows knob.
  If the cosine does not move, aliasing was the wrong diagnosis and v88's
  degradation has another cause that is still unidentified.
  If the cosine recovers but width reaches M+N, the log register has no
  advantage left on this task and the honest conclusion is that the
  linear register is the right choice for Hamiltonian learning.
